{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/94370-detecting-fetches","id":94370,"title":"Detecting Fetches","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-19T12:05:27-07:00","id":94370,"title":"Detecting Fetches","content":"Does anyone know of the various ways to tell if someone's a Fetch? Without killing them (and thus watching their bodies turn in to twigs and pig farts or whatever they happen to be made of) or knowing a Changeling who's clearly the Fetch's original.<br /> <br /> The Dutch of Truth and Loss has their Token, of course. There's also True Sight of St. Abel, available to Hunters of the Malleus Maleficarum, though I'm not REALLY sure how one would describe the effects of using it on a Fetch, as it doesn't really give you specifics (&quot;You sense that the person before you is a constructed copy of the real thing&quot;, perhaps?). Is there anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T12:29:53-07:00","id":94381,"title":"","content":"Exposure to the Hedge reveals a changelings Mien, so if they look like they turn into an Ice person or a Lion fella then they were the Changeling, if they appear the same then they are the fetch. They don't even need to be only in the Hedge if you just get them to cross a portal to the Hedge you can peek in the Portal to find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T16:01:20-07:00","id":94522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/94370-detecting-fetches?p=94381#post94381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exposure to the Hedge reveals a changelings Mien, so if they look like they turn into an Ice person or a Lion fella then they were the Changeling, if they appear the same then they are the fetch. They don't even need to be only in the Hedge if you just get them to cross a portal to the Hedge you can peek in the Portal to find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only really helps to tell the difference between a Changeling and its Fetch though. If you're trying to locate a Fetch from among a variety of other humans, they're pretty hard to spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T16:28:37-07:00","id":94535,"title":"","content":"If a vampire drinks from a fetch, they gain nothing, and suffer from horrifying nightmares when they next sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:11:41-07:00","id":94559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/94370-detecting-fetches?p=94522#post94522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That only really helps to tell the difference between a Changeling and its Fetch though. If you're trying to locate a Fetch from among a variety of other humans, they're pretty hard to spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the point of the thread. How to tell someone apart from their Fetch, rather then just detecting fetches in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:14:07-07:00","id":94560,"title":"","content":"Well, the OP specifically mentions not knowing the Changeling who is clearly the Fetch's double.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:15:51-07:00","id":94564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/94370-detecting-fetches?p=94560#post94560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the OP specifically mentions not knowing the Changeling who is clearly the Fetch's double.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I thought it was talking in context of not know who is the original and who is the double, rather then just hunting lone fetches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:54:52-07:00","id":94579,"title":"","content":"I can't really comment on the intent, but I don't really get that impression from the text. Rather the opposite, in fact.<br /> <br /> Do Fetches show up on a Changeling's Kenning ability? It's been a long while since I read the rules for it, and it wouldn't be a perfect measure if it did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T19:24:17-07:00","id":94629,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry for the confusion -- I meant something along the lines of a person going &quot;I'm going to go hunt Fetches!&quot; for whatever reason, or even a supernatural running in to a Fetch and activating whatever supernatural-detection stuff they were able to use to see what the Fetch (who they currently don't KNOW is a Fetch) is.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all of the responses, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T13:28:41-07:00","id":95181,"title":"","content":"In the Changeling: The Lost corebook, the text under the Kenning heading states that changelings with a Clarity 6 or higher can use Kenning to spot the presence of the supernatural in the area. With a success, the changeling can spot supernatural things (objects, people or effects) that are not being deliberately concealed with magic. Since a fetch is an automaton crafted from detritus and scraps of ephemera masquerading as a person and empowered by fairy glamour, I would assume that its nature would qualify. However, on an Exceptional success at a Kenning test, the changeling becomes sensitive to the presence of even mystically cloaked phenomena. The book states that an Exceptional success is only enough to become aware of a supernatural presence and that it isn't accurate enough to pinpoint its location or identity.<br /> <br /> This is kind of horrifying, if you think about it. Every once in awhile, a changeling can feel the presence of fetch somewhere around her. She looks around at the faces crammed on the subway car with her. Which one of them is it? Do they know? Can they see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T16:12:00-07:00","id":95249,"title":"","content":"The worst part is that Fetches can then see back through the Mask. The Changeling might know there is a Fetch out there, but unless they're alone in a room together they have no idea who it might be. The Fetch though... the Fetch can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:30:53-07:00","id":95609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/94370-detecting-fetches?p=95249#post95249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst part is that Fetches can then see back through the Mask. The Changeling might know there is a Fetch out there, but unless they're alone in a room together they have no idea who it might be. The Fetch though... the Fetch can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that canon? I thought the Fetch could only detect their Original's presence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:03:00-07:00","id":95636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/94370-detecting-fetches?p=95609#post95609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that canon? I thought the Fetch could only detect their Original's presence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. All Fetches begin with the &quot;Attuned to the Wyrd&quot; Echo, which is a magical ability that lets them pierce the Mask as if they were changeling. In addition, they sense the presence of changelings within a 50-foot radius of themselves, although like Kenning, it is a vague sense that lacks specific details (unless, of course, it is the changeling that they are a mirror of ... in that case, the fetch knows exactly who it is).<br /> <br /> There is nothing written about whether or not a changeling strengthening their Mask can be perceived this way, although, IMO, a changeling with a boosted Mask wouldn't trigger any &quot;detect magic&quot; power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T21:46:27-07:00","id":96716,"title":"","content":"I have allowed Kenning to detect Fetches: on a regular success, the changeling just gets the &quot;this is something supernatural&quot; vibe, but on an exceptional success they get, &quot;OMG, FETCH!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1443-murderbunny","name":"Murderbunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T23:05:52-07:00","id":96740,"title":"","content":"I'm going waay out on a limb on this one, very little to support my thinking. So, that's clear.<br /> <br /> Iron. Specifically cold iron. It disrupts pretty much everything to do with the Fae: cuts through Contract protections (at least a couple of which work by disrupting what's seen) or tokens, and usually can't be affected by Fae magic, even doing agg to Fae creatures. What do you think would happen if you touched a Fetch with, say, a cold iron nail? Wouldn't kill them or even really hurt them, but it might disrupt the 'looking normal' magic around them for a second, given that they're constructed out of refuse and Fae magic.<br /> <br /> Tricky to do, of course, but might work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T15:17:40-07:00","id":97074,"title":"","content":"With the rules as written, I don't think iron does anything at all to a Fetch (unless they use Mimic Contract and cast something like Armour of Elements Fury). It doesn't normally affect a Changeling's mask, so I wouldn't think it would do much to a Fetch's (stronger) mask either.<br /> <br /> It's a perfectly valid house rule though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}